Dear {!Contact.FirstName},<br /><br />

Thank you for your interest in the <a href=https://schoolofsustainability.asu.edu/graduate/cass-graduate-certificate.php>complex adaptive systems science (CASS) certificate</a> offered through the School of Sustainability. This certificate is open to any admitted PhD student at ASU. We accept applications for fall or for spring.<br /><br />

If you are not yet a PhD student at ASU, then we recommend you <a href=https://webapp4.asu.edu/programs/t5/graduate/false>look into a program</a>, apply and then meet with the <a href=https://graduate.asu.edu/graduate-faculty/degree/CASS>CASS Faculty</a> once you’re admitted to see if this certificate will help meet your educational objectives. At that point, we recommend you apply, if you are still interested.<br /><br />

We are happy to answer any additional questions you have. To schedule an in-person, phone or Skype appointment, please call our office at 480-727-6963 during our office hours, Monday through Friday, 9a.m. – 4p.m.<br /><br />
 
Regards, <br /><br />

Katerina Kinast <br />
Graduate Academic Success Coordinator <br />
ASU School of Sustainability <br />
